#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""vpn-bot-site — the decoy site behind the REALITY self-steal and the Hysteria2 masquerade
(docs/site.md).

The site is the static tree nginx serves on 127.0.0.1:8443: Xray's REALITY forwards every
TLS client that is not its own there (realitySettings.target), and Hysteria2's masquerade
proxies to the same listener (deploy/hysteria/config.yaml, `type: proxy`). This helper puts
a new version of that tree in place from an archive the superadmin sent the bot, keeps the
versions it replaced and puts one back — never anything else: the nginx configuration and
the certificate are read, never written.

  vpn-bot-site status [--json]                  read-only: the site, its version, its pages,
                                                the kept versions, the spiderX pool
  vpn-bot-site plan deploy --run N --digest D [--json]
                                                takes the bot's upload (UPLOAD_FILE, its
                                                sha256 starting with D), unpacks it into an
                                                isolated directory, checks every entry, and
                                                says what would change (a sha256 of it)
  vpn-bot-site plan revert --run N [--json]     the newest kept version instead
  vpn-bot-site apply --run N --expect-plan SHA [--json]
                                                the plan recomputed (its sha256 must be the
                                                one confirmed), then: the new tree next to
                                                the site → ONE atomic exchange of the two
                                                directories → XRAY_SPIDER_X_POOL of .env;
                                                each step journaled before it acts, any
                                                failure undoes every step
  vpn-bot-site verify --run N [--json]          read-only: GET / and every page 200 over h2
                                                (SNI = the site's domain), ALPN h2 and the
                                                domain's certificate, the tree is the plan's
  vpn-bot-site commit --run N [--json]          verified: the replaced tree is kept (the last
                                                KEEP_RELEASES), state.json says what is live
  vpn-bot-site rollback --run N [--json]        the journal backwards: the old tree back in
                                                place, .env as it was
  vpn-bot-site recover [--json]                 an apply that never finished (its unit was
                                                killed) is rolled back — the wizard's plan
                                                calls it first; one run at a time holds the
                                                wizard's lock, so a journal left open then is
                                                no live run's

WHERE THE SITE IS. Not a constant: the docroot is the `root` of the nginx vhost that listens
on 127.0.0.1:8443 (/etc/nginx/conf.d/*.conf, /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/*) — /var/www/selfsteal
on a host the bot installed (vpn-bot-protocol-install), /var/www/anycastedge on a host set up
by hand. It must be one literal path below /var/www (no variable, not a symlink, a parent
owned by root and writable by nobody else); anything else is refused, the site untouched.

THE ARCHIVE (zip or tar.gz, by its first bytes, not its name), unpacked as root into
/var/lib/vpn-bot-site/work/<run>/ (root 0700) — nothing of it reaches the site before every
entry passed: regular files and directories only (a symlink, a hard link, a device, a FIFO,
a sparse or an encrypted member is refused), a relative path of plain names
([A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9._~-]*: no absolute path, no `..`, no hidden name, no backslash, at
most MAX_DEPTH levels), static files only (STATIC_EXT), at most MAX_FILES files,
MAX_FILE_BYTES each, MAX_TOTAL_BYTES unpacked (counted while reading, not trusted from the
headers), index.html at the top. One folder holding everything (site/index.html, …) is
unwrapped; __MACOSX/ and .DS_Store / Thumbs.db are skipped. The files are written 0644, the
directories 0755, root:root — the archive's modes and owners are ignored.

THE SWAP. The new tree is written next to the docroot (/var/www/.<name>.vpn-bot-site-<run>),
then renameat2(RENAME_EXCHANGE) swaps the two directories in one step: nginx serves the old
site or the new one, never a half. A filesystem without RENAME_EXCHANGE gets two renames
(the docroot away, the new tree in) and the result says so. nginx is not reloaded: it reads
the files per request.

THE SPIDERX POOL. While XRAY_SPIDER_X_POOL is in use (not empty) it follows the site: the
pages of the new tree (/, /about.html, /blog/ for blog/index.html; at most MAX_POOL), so a
REALITY client's spider asks for paths that exist; a path the new site no longer has leaves
the pool. Empty stays empty (spx off is the operator's choice). The keys whose stored spx is
no longer in the pool are re-laid by the BOT after the run (the database is the bot's — this
helper only counts them, read-only); the bot and vpn-bot-subscription read the pool at start,
the wizard's mode restarts them.

STATE: /var/lib/vpn-bot-site/state.json (0644: what is live and what is kept),
journal.json (0600), releases/<id>/ (0700: the kept trees), work/<run>/ (0700).

EXIT CODES: 0 ok · 2 usage · 3 refused (a blocking finding, a plan that changed, an
unfinished apply, nothing to revert to) · 4 verify failed · 5 cannot (a tool, a file) · 6 a
step failed and the rollback succeeded · 7 a step failed and the rollback did not fully
succeed.

Stdlib only, every command an argv list (never a shell). TEST SEAM (never in production;
sudo and systemd-run give a clean environment): VPN_BOT_SITE_SELFTEST=1 needs
VPN_BOT_SITE_ROOT (every host path under it, nothing is written outside it — the test suite
also runs as root on the production host) and VPN_BOT_SITE_SELFTEST_BIN (the only commands
that run), skips chown and the root-ownership checks; _SELFTEST_FAIL=<step> fails right after
that step did its work, _SELFTEST_NO_EXCHANGE=1 takes the two-rename path.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import contextlib
import ctypes
import errno
import fcntl
import gzip
import hashlib
import io
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import sqlite3
import stat
import subprocess  # noqa: S404 — fixed argv lists of curl / openssl / systemctl, never a shell
import sys
import tarfile
import tempfile
import time
import zipfile
from collections.abc import Callable, Iterator, Mapping, Sequence
from dataclasses import dataclass, field
from pathlib import Path
from typing import IO, Any
from urllib.parse import quote

SELFTEST = os.environ.get("VPN_BOT_SITE_SELFTEST") == "1"
HELPER_VERSION = 1

EXIT_OK, EXIT_USAGE, EXIT_REFUSED, EXIT_VERIFY, EXIT_CANNOT, EXIT_ROLLED_BACK, EXIT_ROLLBACK_FAILED = 0, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7

APP_DIR = "/opt/vpn-service"
ENV_FILE = f"{APP_DIR}/.env"
DEFAULT_DB = f"{APP_DIR}/data/vpn.db"
STATE_DIR = "/var/lib/vpn-bot-site"
STATE_FILE = f"{STATE_DIR}/state.json"
JOURNAL_FILE = f"{STATE_DIR}/journal.json"
RELEASES_DIR = f"{STATE_DIR}/releases"
WORK_DIR = f"{STATE_DIR}/work"
# Where the bot puts the archive it received (its RuntimeDirectory, deploy/vpn-bot.service;
# the same fixed staging root as /run/vpn-bot/xray of vpn-bot-xray-apply). Read once, with
# O_NOFOLLOW, copied into WORK_DIR and removed: nothing after the plan reads the bot's copy.
UPLOAD_DIR = "/run/vpn-bot/site"
UPLOAD_FILE = f"{UPLOAD_DIR}/upload.bin"
LOCK_FILE = "/run/vpn-bot-site.lock"
LOG_FILE = "/var/log/vpn-bot-site.log"
NGINX_CONF_DIRS = (("/etc/nginx/conf.d", ".conf"), ("/etc/nginx/sites-enabled", ""))
HY2_CONFIG = "/etc/hysteria/config.yaml"
DOCROOT_BASE = "/var/www"
SELFSTEAL_PORT = 8443
SELFSTEAL_ADDR = f"127.0.0.1:{SELFSTEAL_PORT}"
SELFSTEAL_LISTENS = frozenset({SELFSTEAL_ADDR, str(SELFSTEAL_PORT), f"*:{SELFSTEAL_PORT}", f"0.0.0.0:{SELFSTEAL_PORT}"})
NGINX_UNIT = "nginx.service"
POOL_KEY = "XRAY_SPIDER_X_POOL"
COMMAND_TIMEOUT = 60

# The archive. MAX_ARCHIVE_BYTES is the Bot API's download limit (services/site.py refuses
# a bigger document before it is downloaded; a test keeps the two equal).
MAX_ARCHIVE_BYTES = 20 << 20
MAX_TOTAL_BYTES = 64 << 20
MAX_FILE_BYTES = 16 << 20
MAX_FILES = 1000
MAX_DEPTH = 12
MAX_PATH = 512
# Static files only: pages, styles, scripts, images, fonts, xml, txt.
STATIC_EXT = frozenset({
    ".html", ".htm", ".css", ".js", ".mjs", ".xml", ".txt",
    ".svg", ".png", ".jpg", ".jpeg", ".gif", ".webp", ".avif", ".ico", ".bmp",
    ".woff", ".woff2", ".ttf", ".otf", ".eot",
})
PAGE_EXT = (".html", ".htm")
JUNK_DIRS = frozenset({"__MACOSX"})
JUNK_FILES = frozenset({".DS_Store", "Thumbs.db"})
_NAME_RE = re.compile(r"^[A-Za-z0-9_][A-Za-z0-9._~-]{0,127}$")
# A pool entry is a path a link carries as spx (quoted) and .env holds comma-separated.
_POOL_PATH_RE = re.compile(r"^/[A-Za-z0-9._~/-]{0,255}$")
_DIGEST_RE = re.compile(r"^[0-9a-f]{16}$")
_SHA_RE = re.compile(r"^[0-9a-f]{64}$")
_DNS_NAME_RE = re.compile(r"^(?=.{1,253}$)([a-z0-9](?:[a-z0-9-]{0,61}[a-z0-9])?\.)+[a-z]{2,63}$")
_ENV_LINE_RE = re.compile(r"^\s*(?:export\s+)?([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\s*=\s*(.*)$")

KEEP_RELEASES = 5
MAX_POOL = 64
MAX_LISTED = 300
# A tree this helper did not write (the hand-made site) is hashed up to here.
SCAN_MAX_FILES = 20000
SCAN_MAX_BYTES = 1 << 30
CURL_BATCH = 40
APPLY_STEPS = ("site_stage", "site_swap", "site_env")

# vpn-bot-wizard-lib's redaction (utils/redact.py): every line of the log goes through it.
_REDACT = (
    (re.compile(r"(?i)(secret=)[^&\s]+"), r"\1***"),
    (re.compile(r"\b(bot_token|token|password|passwd|secret|mtproto_secret|private_key|preshared_key)\s*([:=])\s*[^,\s;]+", re.I), r"\1\2***"),
    (re.compile(r"\b(?:dd)?[0-9a-fA-F]{32,}\b"), "***"),
    (re.compile(r"\b\d{8,12}:[A-Za-z0-9_-]{35}\b"), "***"),
    (re.compile(r"(?i)\bBearer\s+[A-Za-z0-9_.~+/=-]{16,}\b"), "Bearer ***"),
    (re.compile(r"(?i)([a-z][a-z0-9+\-.]*://)([^:@/\s]+:[^@/\s]+@)"), r"\1***@"),
    (re.compile(r"\b[A-Za-z0-9+/]{43}={1,2}(?=[^A-Za-z0-9+/=]|$)"), "***"),
)


def redact(text: str) -> str:
    for pattern, repl in _REDACT:
        text = pattern.sub(repl, text)
    return text


class Refused(Exception):
    """A finding that stops the run before anything changes (exit 3)."""


class Cannot(Exception):
    """A tool, a file or a directory that is not there or not usable (exit 5)."""


class StepFailed(Exception):
    def __init__(self, step: str, message: str) -> None:
        super().__init__(message)
        self.step = step


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Context: host paths, commands, the log
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
@dataclass
class Ctx:
    root: str
    bin_dir: str
    fail_at: str
    no_exchange: bool
    json_out: bool = False
    log_lines: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)

    def host(self, path: str) -> Path:
        return Path(self.root.rstrip("/") + path) if self.root else Path(path)

    def unroot(self, path: Path | str) -> str:
        text = str(path)
        if self.root and text.startswith(self.root.rstrip("/") + "/"):
            return text[len(self.root.rstrip("/")):]
        return text

    def log(self, text: str) -> None:
        line = redact(text)
        self.log_lines.append(line)
        with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
            lf = self.host(LOG_FILE)
            lf.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
            with open(lf, "a", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
                for part in line.splitlines() or [""]:
                    fh.write(f"{iso_now()} {part}\n")

    def say(self, text: str) -> None:
        self.log(text)
        if not self.json_out:
            print(text)

    def event(self, **fields: Any) -> None:
        """A JSON line the wizard's mode reads as it comes (``{"event": "step", ...}``)."""
        if self.json_out:
            print(json.dumps(fields, sort_keys=True), flush=True)


def make_ctx(json_out: bool) -> Ctx:
    if SELFTEST:
        root = os.environ.get("VPN_BOT_SITE_ROOT", "")
        bin_dir = os.environ.get("VPN_BOT_SITE_SELFTEST_BIN", "")
        if not root or os.path.realpath(root) == "/" or not os.path.isdir(root):
            raise Refused("selftest: VPN_BOT_SITE_ROOT must be an existing directory other than /")
        if not bin_dir or not os.path.isdir(bin_dir):
            raise Refused("selftest: VPN_BOT_SITE_SELFTEST_BIN must be a directory of stubs")
        return Ctx(root=os.path.realpath(root), bin_dir=os.path.realpath(bin_dir),
                   fail_at=os.environ.get("VPN_BOT_SITE_SELFTEST_FAIL", ""),
                   no_exchange=os.environ.get("VPN_BOT_SITE_SELFTEST_NO_EXCHANGE") == "1", json_out=json_out)
    return Ctx(root="", bin_dir="", fail_at="", no_exchange=False, json_out=json_out)


def iso_now() -> str:
    return time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime())


def fence(ctx: Ctx, path: Path) -> None:
    """Under the seam nothing outside the fake root is ever written or removed."""
    if ctx.root and not os.path.abspath(path).startswith(ctx.root.rstrip("/") + "/"):
        raise Cannot(f"selftest: refusing to touch {path} outside the fake root")


def tool(ctx: Ctx, name: str) -> str | None:
    if not SELFTEST:
        return name
    path = os.path.join(ctx.bin_dir, os.path.basename(name))
    return path if os.path.isfile(path) and os.access(path, os.X_OK) else None


def run(ctx: Ctx, argv: Sequence[str], *, timeout: int = COMMAND_TIMEOUT, stdin: str | None = None) -> tuple[int, str]:
    """(exit code, stdout+stderr). 127 = not found / refused, 124 = timed out."""
    exe = tool(ctx, argv[0])
    if exe is None:
        ctx.log(f"$ {' '.join(argv)}\n  refused under the selftest: no stub {argv[0]}")
        return 127, f"{argv[0]}: refused (selftest: not a stub)"
    env = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k not in ("LANGUAGE", "LC_MESSAGES")}
    env["LC_ALL"] = "C"
    if not SELFTEST:
        env["PATH"] = "/usr/local/sbin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin"
    try:
        proc = subprocess.run(  # noqa: S603 — argv list, never a shell
            [exe, *argv[1:]], input=stdin, capture_output=True, text=True, errors="replace",
            timeout=timeout, check=False, env=env, stdin=None if stdin is not None else subprocess.DEVNULL,
        )
    except FileNotFoundError:
        ctx.log(f"$ {' '.join(argv)}\n  not found")
        return 127, f"{argv[0]}: not found"
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired as exc:
        out = exc.stdout if isinstance(exc.stdout, str) else ""
        ctx.log(f"$ {' '.join(argv)}\n  timed out after {timeout}s")
        return 124, f"{out}\n{argv[0]}: timed out after {timeout}s"
    out = (proc.stdout or "") + (proc.stderr or "")
    ctx.log(f"$ {' '.join(argv[:12])}{' …' if len(argv) > 12 else ''}  (exit {proc.returncode})\n{out.rstrip()[-2000:]}")
    return proc.returncode, out


@contextlib.contextmanager
def helper_lock(ctx: Ctx) -> Iterator[None]:
    path = ctx.host(LOCK_FILE)
    fence(ctx, path)
    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT | os.O_NOFOLLOW, 0o600)
    try:
        try:
            fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
        except BlockingIOError:
            raise Refused("another vpn-bot-site run holds its lock") from None
        yield
    finally:
        os.close(fd)


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Files
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
def write_file(ctx: Ctx, path: Path, data: bytes, mode: int, *, uid: int | None = None, gid: int | None = None) -> None:
    """Atomic: a temporary file next to the target, mode (and owner) set before the rename."""
    fence(ctx, path)
    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=str(path.parent), prefix=f".{path.name}.vpn-bot-site-")
    try:
        os.fchmod(fd, mode)
        if not SELFTEST and os.geteuid() == 0 and uid is not None and gid is not None:
            os.fchown(fd, uid, gid)
        with os.fdopen(fd, "wb") as fh:
            fh.write(data)
            fh.flush()
            os.fsync(fh.fileno())
        os.replace(tmp, path)
    except BaseException:
        with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
            os.unlink(tmp)
        raise


def ensure_dir(ctx: Ctx, path: Path, mode: int) -> None:
    fence(ctx, path)
    if path.is_symlink():
        raise Cannot(f"{ctx.unroot(path)} is a symlink")
    path.mkdir(mode=mode, parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    os.chmod(path, mode)


def remove_tree(ctx: Ctx, path: Path) -> None:
    fence(ctx, path)
    if path.is_symlink() or path.is_file():
        path.unlink()
    elif path.is_dir():
        shutil.rmtree(path)


def copy_tree(ctx: Ctx, src: Path, dst: Path) -> None:
    """A kept tree back next to the docroot: symlinks as symlinks, modes and (as root)
    owners as they were — what nginx served before is what it serves again."""
    fence(ctx, dst)
    shutil.copytree(src, dst, symlinks=True, copy_function=shutil.copy2)
    if SELFTEST or os.geteuid() != 0:
        return
    for base, dirs, files in os.walk(src):
        rel = os.path.relpath(base, src)
        for name in [".", *dirs, *files] if rel == "." else [*dirs, *files]:
            s = os.path.join(base, name) if name != "." else base
            d = os.path.join(dst, rel, name) if name != "." else os.path.join(dst, rel)
            st = os.lstat(s)
            os.lchown(os.path.normpath(d), st.st_uid, st.st_gid)


def move_tree(ctx: Ctx, src: Path, dst: Path) -> None:
    """rename, or (another filesystem) copy then remove."""
    fence(ctx, src)
    fence(ctx, dst)
    try:
        os.rename(src, dst)
    except OSError as exc:
        if exc.errno != errno.EXDEV:
            raise
        copy_tree(ctx, src, dst)
        shutil.rmtree(src)


_RENAME_EXCHANGE = 2
_AT_FDCWD = -100


def exchange(ctx: Ctx, a: Path, b: Path) -> bool:
    """Swap two directories in one step (renameat2 RENAME_EXCHANGE). False: the kernel or
    the filesystem cannot (the caller takes two renames)."""
    fence(ctx, a)
    fence(ctx, b)
    if ctx.no_exchange:
        return False
    try:
        libc = ctypes.CDLL(None, use_errno=True)
        fn = libc.renameat2
    except (OSError, AttributeError):
        return False
    fn.argtypes = [ctypes.c_int, ctypes.c_char_p, ctypes.c_int, ctypes.c_char_p, ctypes.c_uint]
    fn.restype = ctypes.c_int
    if fn(_AT_FDCWD, os.fsencode(str(a)), _AT_FDCWD, os.fsencode(str(b)), _RENAME_EXCHANGE) == 0:
        return True
    err = ctypes.get_errno()
    if err in (errno.EINVAL, errno.ENOSYS, errno.EOPNOTSUPP, errno.ENOTSUP):
        return False
    raise OSError(err, os.strerror(err), str(a))


def root_owned_dir(ctx: Ctx, path: Path) -> str | None:
    """Why *path* cannot hold a directory root swaps in, or None."""
    try:
        st = os.lstat(path)
    except OSError as exc:
        return f"{ctx.unroot(path)}: {exc.strerror}"
    if stat.S_ISLNK(st.st_mode) or not stat.S_ISDIR(st.st_mode):
        return f"{ctx.unroot(path)} is not a directory"
    if not SELFTEST and (st.st_uid != 0 or st.st_mode & 0o022):
        return f"{ctx.unroot(path)} must be root-owned and writable by root only (uid {st.st_uid}, mode {st.st_mode & 0o7777:04o})"
    return None


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# .env — the tolerant reader of every helper (`export`, spaces around `=`, one pair of
# quotes, an inline comment; the LAST assignment wins). Never sourced.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
def env_value(raw: str) -> str:
    value = raw.strip()
    if value[:1] in ("'", '"'):
        q = value[0]
        end = value.find(q, 1)
        return value[1:end] if end > 0 else value[1:]
    return re.sub(r"\s+#.*$", "", value).strip()


def read_env_text(text: str) -> dict[str, str]:
    values: dict[str, str] = {}
    for line in text.splitlines():
        m = _ENV_LINE_RE.match(line)
        if m:
            values[m.group(1)] = env_value(m.group(2))
    return values


def read_env(ctx: Ctx) -> dict[str, str]:
    try:
        return read_env_text(ctx.host(ENV_FILE).read_text(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace"))
    except OSError:
        return {}


def edit_env_text(text: str, updates: Mapping[str, str]) -> str:
    """*text* with each key's LAST assignment replaced (`KEY=value`), or the line appended.
    Every other line stays byte for byte (vpn-bot-protocol-install's rule)."""
    lines = text.splitlines(keepends=True)
    last: dict[str, int] = {}
    for i, line in enumerate(lines):
        m = _ENV_LINE_RE.match(line)
        if m and m.group(1) in updates:
            last[m.group(1)] = i
    out = list(lines)
    appended: list[str] = []
    for key, value in updates.items():
        if key in last:
            i = last[key]
            out[i] = f"{key}={value}" + ("\n" if lines[i].endswith("\n") else "")
        else:
            appended.append(f"{key}={value}\n")
    if appended:
        if out and not out[-1].endswith("\n"):
            out[-1] += "\n"
        out.extend(appended)
    return "".join(out)


def parse_pool(raw: str | None) -> list[str]:
    """utils/spider_x.parse_spider_x_pool, and only entries the settings layer accepts."""
    if not raw:
        return []
    return [p.strip() for p in raw.split(",") if p.strip() and p.strip().startswith("/")]


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# nginx: the vhost on 127.0.0.1:8443 (read, never written)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
_TOKEN_RE = re.compile(r'"(?:[^"\\]|\\.)*"|\'(?:[^\'\\]|\\.)*\'|[{};]|[^\s{};"\']+')


@dataclass
class Directive:
    name: str
    args: list[str]
    children: list[Directive] | None = None


def _unquote(tok: str) -> str:
    if len(tok) >= 2 and tok[0] == tok[-1] and tok[0] in "\"'":
        return tok[1:-1]
    return tok


def parse_nginx(text: str) -> list[Directive]:
    lines = []
    for line in text.splitlines():
        out, quote_ch = [], ""
        for ch in line:
            if quote_ch:
                out.append(ch)
                if ch == quote_ch:
                    quote_ch = ""
            elif ch in "\"'":
                quote_ch = ch
                out.append(ch)
            elif ch == "#":
                break
            else:
                out.append(ch)
        lines.append("".join(out))
    top: list[Directive] = []
    stack: list[list[Directive]] = [top]
    cur: list[str] = []
    for tok in _TOKEN_RE.findall("\n".join(lines)):
        if tok == ";":
            if cur:
                stack[-1].append(Directive(cur[0], cur[1:]))
            cur = []
        elif tok == "{":
            block = Directive(cur[0] if cur else "", cur[1:], [])
            stack[-1].append(block)
            assert block.children is not None
            stack.append(block.children)
            cur = []
        elif tok == "}":
            if len(stack) > 1:
                stack.pop()
            cur = []
        else:
            cur.append(_unquote(tok))
    return top


def _servers(directives: list[Directive]) -> Iterator[Directive]:
    for d in directives:
        if d.children is None:
            continue
        if d.name == "server":
            yield d
        else:
            yield from _servers(d.children)


def nginx_conf_files(ctx: Ctx) -> list[Path]:
    files: list[Path] = []
    for d, suffix in NGINX_CONF_DIRS:
        base = ctx.host(d)
        if base.is_dir():
            files += sorted(p for p in base.iterdir() if p.is_file() and (not suffix or p.name.endswith(suffix)))
    return files


@dataclass
class Site:
    docroot: str          # host path (unrooted)
    domain: str
    vhost: str            # the config file (unrooted)
    exists: bool


def discover(ctx: Ctx) -> tuple[Site | None, list[str]]:
    """The vhost that listens on 127.0.0.1:8443 and its docroot; the reasons it cannot be used."""
    found: list[tuple[Path, Directive]] = []
    for f in nginx_conf_files(ctx):
        try:
            text = f.read_text(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")
        except OSError:
            continue
        for server in _servers(parse_nginx(text)):
            assert server.children is not None
            listens = [d for d in server.children if d.name == "listen" and d.args]
            if any(d.args[0] in SELFSTEAL_LISTENS for d in listens):
                found.append((f, server))
    if not found:
        return None, [f"no nginx vhost listens on {SELFSTEAL_ADDR} (the REALITY self-steal) — install Xray from the bot first"]
    if len(found) > 1:
        return None, [f"{len(found)} nginx vhosts listen on {SELFSTEAL_ADDR}: "
                      + ", ".join(ctx.unroot(f) for f, _ in found) + " — which one is the site cannot be told"]
    f, server = found[0]
    assert server.children is not None
    roots = [d.args[0] for d in server.children if d.name == "root" and d.args]
    for loc in server.children:
        if loc.name == "location" and loc.args == ["/"] and loc.children is not None:
            roots += [d.args[0] for d in loc.children if d.name == "root" and d.args]
    vhost = ctx.unroot(f)
    if not roots:
        return None, [f"{vhost}: the vhost on {SELFSTEAL_ADDR} has no `root`"]
    if len(set(roots)) > 1:
        return None, [f"{vhost}: more than one `root` ({', '.join(sorted(set(roots)))})"]
    docroot = roots[0]
    names = [n.lower() for d in server.children if d.name == "server_name" for n in d.args]
    domain = next((n for n in names if _DNS_NAME_RE.match(n)), "")
    if not domain:
        env_sni = read_env(ctx).get("HYSTERIA2_SNI", "").strip().lower()
        domain = env_sni if _DNS_NAME_RE.match(env_sni) else ""
    problems = []
    if "$" in docroot:
        problems.append(f"{vhost}: root {docroot} is not a literal path")
    elif not docroot.startswith("/") or os.path.normpath(docroot) != docroot.rstrip("/") or \
            not docroot.startswith(DOCROOT_BASE + "/") or docroot.rstrip("/") == DOCROOT_BASE:
        problems.append(f"{vhost}: root {docroot} is not a directory below {DOCROOT_BASE}/ — the helper swaps only there")
    docroot = docroot.rstrip("/")
    if not domain:
        problems.append(f"{vhost}: no server_name and no HYSTERIA2_SNI — the site's domain (its SNI) cannot be told")
    if any(d.name == "listen" and d.args and d.args[0] in SELFSTEAL_LISTENS and "proxy_protocol" in d.args
           for d in server.children):
        # Xray's REALITY with xver sends a PROXY header first: openssl / curl on loopback
        # cannot speak it, so neither the checks before the change nor verify could tell a
        # working site from a broken one.
        problems.append(f"{vhost}: the vhost on {SELFSTEAL_ADDR} expects the PROXY protocol (Xray `xver`) — "
                        "the helper's checks cannot reach it directly")
    host_root = ctx.host(docroot)
    exists = host_root.exists() or host_root.is_symlink()
    if not problems:
        if host_root.is_symlink():
            problems.append(f"{docroot} is a symlink — the helper swaps a directory, not a link")
        elif exists and not host_root.is_dir():
            problems.append(f"{docroot} exists and is not a directory")
        else:
            why = root_owned_dir(ctx, host_root.parent)
            if why:
                problems.append(why)
    return Site(docroot=docroot, domain=domain, vhost=vhost, exists=exists), problems


def hy2_layout(ctx: Ctx) -> dict[str, str]:
    """How Hysteria2's masquerade reaches a site: the same listener (proxy) or a copy (file)."""
    try:
        text = ctx.host(HY2_CONFIG).read_text(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")
    except OSError:
        return {"layout": "absent", "detail": ""}
    lines = text.splitlines()
    start = next((i for i, line in enumerate(lines) if re.match(r"^masquerade:\s*(#.*)?$", line)), None)
    if start is None:
        return {"layout": "none", "detail": ""}
    body = []
    for line in lines[start + 1:]:
        if line.strip() and not line[:1].isspace() and not line.lstrip().startswith("#"):
            break
        body.append(line)
    block = "\n".join(body)
    kind = re.search(r"^[ \t]+type:\s*([A-Za-z]+)", block, re.MULTILINE)
    layout = kind.group(1).lower() if kind else "unknown"
    if layout == "proxy":
        url = re.search(r"^[ \t]+url:\s*(\S+)", block, re.MULTILINE)
        target = url.group(1) if url else ""
        return {"layout": "proxy" if SELFSTEAL_ADDR in target else "other", "detail": target}
    if layout == "file":
        d = re.search(r"^[ \t]+dir:\s*(\S+)", block, re.MULTILINE)
        return {"layout": "file", "detail": d.group(1) if d else ""}
    return {"layout": layout, "detail": ""}


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Trees: a hash of every regular file, the pages
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
@dataclass
class Tree:
    files: dict[str, tuple[str, int]] = field(default_factory=dict)   # rel -> (sha256, size)
    symlinks: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)
    others: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)
    complete: bool = True
    newest: float = 0.0

    @property
    def digest(self) -> str:
        if not self.complete:
            return ""
        h = hashlib.sha256()
        for rel in sorted(self.files):
            h.update(f"{rel}\0{self.files[rel][0]}\n".encode())
        for rel in sorted(self.symlinks):
            h.update(f"{rel}\0->\n".encode())
        return h.hexdigest()

    @property
    def size(self) -> int:
        return sum(size for _, size in self.files.values())

    def pages(self) -> list[str]:
        return pages_of(self.files)


def page_url(rel: str) -> str:
    if rel == "index.html":
        return "/"
    if rel.endswith("/index.html"):
        return "/" + rel[: -len("index.html")]
    return "/" + rel


def pages_of(files: Mapping[str, object] | Sequence[str]) -> list[str]:
    urls = {page_url(rel) for rel in files if rel.lower().endswith(PAGE_EXT)}
    return sorted(urls, key=lambda u: (u != "/", u))


def file_sha256(path: Path) -> str:
    h = hashlib.sha256()
    fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW)
    with os.fdopen(fd, "rb") as fh:
        for chunk in iter(lambda: fh.read(1 << 20), b""):
            h.update(chunk)
    return h.hexdigest()


def scan_tree(base: Path) -> Tree:
    tree = Tree()
    if not base.is_dir() or base.is_symlink():
        return tree
    total = 0
    for cur, dirs, files in os.walk(base, followlinks=False):
        rel_dir = os.path.relpath(cur, base)
        for name in sorted(dirs):
            if os.path.islink(os.path.join(cur, name)):
                tree.symlinks.append(os.path.normpath(os.path.join(rel_dir, name)))
        dirs[:] = sorted(d for d in dirs if not os.path.islink(os.path.join(cur, d)))
        for name in sorted(files):
            fp = Path(cur) / name
            rel = os.path.normpath(os.path.join(rel_dir, name))
            st = os.lstat(fp)
            if stat.S_ISLNK(st.st_mode):
                tree.symlinks.append(rel)
                continue
            if not stat.S_ISREG(st.st_mode):
                tree.others.append(rel)
                continue
            if len(tree.files) >= SCAN_MAX_FILES or total + st.st_size > SCAN_MAX_BYTES:
                tree.complete = False
                return tree
            total += st.st_size
            tree.newest = max(tree.newest, st.st_mtime)
            tree.files[rel] = (file_sha256(fp), st.st_size)
    return tree


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# The archive: unpacked as root into an isolated directory, every entry checked first
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
@dataclass
class Unpacked:
    tree: Path                # the site's top (after an unwrapped folder)
    unwrapped: str = ""
    skipped: int = 0
    files: int = 0
    size: int = 0


def member_path(raw: str, *, is_dir: bool) -> str | None:
    """The checked relative path of an archive entry; "" for the archive's own top ("./"),
    None for junk that is skipped (__MACOSX/, .DS_Store, Thumbs.db)."""
    if "\x00" in raw or "\\" in raw:
        raise Refused(f"{raw[:120]!r}: a backslash or NUL in the name")
    if raw.startswith("/"):
        raise Refused(f"{raw[:120]!r}: an absolute path")
    parts = raw.split("/")
    while parts and parts[0] == ".":
        parts.pop(0)
    if parts and parts[-1] == "":
        parts.pop()
    if not parts:
        return ""
    if parts[0] in JUNK_DIRS or (not is_dir and parts[-1] in JUNK_FILES):
        return None
    for p in parts:
        if p in ("", ".", ".."):
            raise Refused(f"{raw[:120]!r}: `..`, `.` or an empty part in the path")
        if not _NAME_RE.match(p):
            raise Refused(f"{raw[:120]!r}: {p[:60]!r} is not a plain name ([A-Za-z0-9_] then [A-Za-z0-9._~-]; no hidden names)")
    if len(parts) > MAX_DEPTH:
        raise Refused(f"{raw[:120]!r}: deeper than {MAX_DEPTH} levels")
    rel = "/".join(parts)
    if len(rel) > MAX_PATH:
        raise Refused(f"{raw[:120]!r}: a path longer than {MAX_PATH}")
    if not is_dir:
        ext = os.path.splitext(parts[-1])[1].lower()
        if ext not in STATIC_EXT:
            raise Refused(f"{rel}: not a static file of the site ({', '.join(sorted(STATIC_EXT))})")
    return rel


class _Budget:
    def __init__(self) -> None:
        self.files = 0
        self.size = 0

    def file(self, rel: str, declared: int) -> None:
        self.files += 1
        if self.files > MAX_FILES:
            raise Refused(f"more than {MAX_FILES} files")
        if declared > MAX_FILE_BYTES:
            raise Refused(f"{rel}: {declared} bytes, more than {MAX_FILE_BYTES} per file")
        if self.size + max(declared, 0) > MAX_TOTAL_BYTES:
            raise Refused(f"more than {MAX_TOTAL_BYTES} bytes unpacked")

    def add(self, rel: str, n: int, written: int) -> None:
        self.size += n
        if written > MAX_FILE_BYTES:
            raise Refused(f"{rel}: more than {MAX_FILE_BYTES} bytes")
        if self.size > MAX_TOTAL_BYTES:
            raise Refused(f"more than {MAX_TOTAL_BYTES} bytes unpacked")


def _mkdirs(base: Path, rel: str) -> Path:
    cur = base
    for part in rel.split("/"):
        cur = cur / part
        try:
            os.mkdir(cur, 0o755)
        except FileExistsError:
            if cur.is_symlink() or not cur.is_dir():
                raise Refused(f"{rel}: a file and a directory of the same name") from None
        else:
            os.chmod(cur, 0o755)  # noqa: S103 — a directory of the site: nginx reads it
    return cur


def _write_member(base: Path, rel: str, src: IO[bytes], budget: _Budget, declared: int) -> None:
    parent = rel.rsplit("/", 1)[0] if "/" in rel else ""
    if parent:
        _mkdirs(base, parent)
    target = base / rel
    try:
        fd = os.open(target, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL | os.O_NOFOLLOW, 0o644)
    except FileExistsError:
        raise Refused(f"{rel}: twice in the archive (or a file and a directory of the same name)") from None
    written = 0
    with os.fdopen(fd, "wb") as out:
        while True:
            chunk = src.read(1 << 16)
            if not chunk:
                break
            written += len(chunk)
            if declared >= 0 and written > declared:
                raise Refused(f"{rel}: more data than its header says")
            budget.add(rel, len(chunk), written)
            out.write(chunk)
    os.chmod(target, 0o644)


class _Limited(io.RawIOBase):
    """The decompressed stream, cut off past *limit* bytes (a gzip bomb never fills a disk)."""

    def __init__(self, inner: IO[bytes], limit: int) -> None:
        self.inner = inner
        self.limit = limit
        self.seen = 0

    def readable(self) -> bool:
        return True

    def readinto(self, b: Any) -> int:
        data = self.inner.read(len(b))
        self.seen += len(data)
        if self.seen > self.limit:
            raise Refused(f"more than {MAX_TOTAL_BYTES} bytes unpacked")
        b[: len(data)] = data
        return len(data)


def _unpack_zip(archive: Path, dest: Path, budget: _Budget) -> int:
    skipped = 0
    try:
        zf = zipfile.ZipFile(archive)
    except (zipfile.BadZipFile, OSError) as exc:
        raise Refused(f"not a readable zip: {exc}") from None
    with zf:
        infos = zf.infolist()
        if len(infos) > MAX_FILES * 2:
            raise Refused(f"more than {MAX_FILES} files")
        seen: set[str] = set()
        for info in infos:
            mode = info.external_attr >> 16
            is_dir = info.is_dir() or (info.create_system == 3 and stat.S_ISDIR(mode))
            # A Unix zip carries the file type in the high bits; without one (Windows zips,
            # Python's writestr: permissions only) the entry is a file or, by its name, a dir.
            if info.create_system == 3 and stat.S_IFMT(mode):
                if stat.S_ISLNK(mode):
                    raise Refused(f"{info.filename[:120]!r}: a symlink")
                if not (stat.S_ISREG(mode) or stat.S_ISDIR(mode)):
                    raise Refused(f"{info.filename[:120]!r}: not a regular file or a directory")
            if info.flag_bits & 0x1:
                raise Refused(f"{info.filename[:120]!r}: encrypted")
            rel = member_path(info.filename, is_dir=is_dir)
            if not rel:
                skipped += rel is None
                continue
            if rel in seen:
                raise Refused(f"{rel}: twice in the archive")
            seen.add(rel)
            if is_dir:
                _mkdirs(dest, rel)
                continue
            if info.compress_type not in (zipfile.ZIP_STORED, zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED):
                raise Refused(f"{rel}: compression method {info.compress_type} (only stored / deflated)")
            budget.file(rel, info.file_size)
            try:
                with zf.open(info) as src:
                    _write_member(dest, rel, src, budget, info.file_size)
            except (zipfile.BadZipFile, zlib_error(), EOFError) as exc:
                raise Refused(f"{rel}: {exc}") from None
    return skipped


def zlib_error() -> type[Exception]:
    import zlib

    return zlib.error


def _unpack_tar_gz(archive: Path, dest: Path, budget: _Budget) -> int:
    skipped = 0
    limit = MAX_TOTAL_BYTES + (MAX_FILES + 64) * 3 * 512 + (1 << 20)
    try:
        with open(archive, "rb") as raw, gzip.GzipFile(fileobj=raw) as gz:
            stream = io.BufferedReader(_Limited(gz, limit))  # type: ignore[arg-type]
            with tarfile.open(fileobj=stream, mode="r|") as tar:
                seen: set[str] = set()
                for member in tar:
                    if member.issym():
                        raise Refused(f"{member.name[:120]!r}: a symlink")
                    if member.islnk():
                        raise Refused(f"{member.name[:120]!r}: a hard link")
                    if member.issparse():
                        raise Refused(f"{member.name[:120]!r}: a sparse file")
                    if not (member.isreg() or member.isdir()):
                        raise Refused(f"{member.name[:120]!r}: not a regular file or a directory (a device, a FIFO, …)")
                    rel = member_path(member.name, is_dir=member.isdir())
                    if not rel:
                        skipped += rel is None
                        continue
                    if rel in seen and not member.isdir():
                        raise Refused(f"{rel}: twice in the archive")
                    seen.add(rel)
                    if member.isdir():
                        _mkdirs(dest, rel)
                        continue
                    budget.file(rel, member.size)
                    src = tar.extractfile(member)
                    if src is None:
                        raise Refused(f"{rel}: unreadable member")
                    _write_member(dest, rel, src, budget, member.size)
    except (tarfile.TarError, OSError, EOFError, zlib_error()) as exc:
        raise Refused(f"not a readable tar.gz: {exc}") from None
    return skipped


def archive_kind(path: Path) -> str:
    with open(path, "rb") as fh:
        head = fh.read(4)
    if head[:4] in (b"PK\x03\x04", b"PK\x05\x06"):
        return "zip"
    if head[:2] == b"\x1f\x8b":
        return "tar.gz"
    raise Refused("the file is neither a zip nor a tar.gz (by its first bytes)")


def unpack(ctx: Ctx, archive: Path, dest: Path) -> Unpacked:
    """Every entry checked BEFORE it is written; *dest* is a fresh root-only directory."""
    fence(ctx, dest)
    if dest.exists():
        shutil.rmtree(dest)
    dest.mkdir(mode=0o700, parents=False)
    raw = dest / "raw"
    raw.mkdir(mode=0o755)
    os.chmod(raw, 0o755)  # noqa: S103 — a directory of the site: nginx reads it
    budget = _Budget()
    kind = archive_kind(archive)
    skipped = _unpack_zip(archive, raw, budget) if kind == "zip" else _unpack_tar_gz(archive, raw, budget)
    top = raw
    unwrapped = ""
    if not (raw / "index.html").is_file():
        entries = list(raw.iterdir())
        if len(entries) == 1 and entries[0].is_dir() and (entries[0] / "index.html").is_file():
            top = entries[0]
            unwrapped = entries[0].name + "/"
    if not (top / "index.html").is_file():
        raise Refused("no index.html at the top of the archive (or in its one folder)")
    os.chmod(top, 0o755)  # noqa: S103 — a directory of the site: nginx reads it
    return Unpacked(tree=top, unwrapped=unwrapped, skipped=skipped, files=budget.files, size=budget.size)


def take_upload(ctx: Ctx, digest: str, work: Path) -> tuple[Path, str]:
    """The bot's upload, read once (O_NOFOLLOW, a regular file, the digest it announced),
    copied into the run's root-only directory and removed."""
    # The bot owns its RuntimeDirectory and could swap `site` for a symlink: the directory
    # is opened with O_NOFOLLOW and the file relative to it, so root reads a regular file
    # of THAT directory or nothing (/run and /run/vpn-bot themselves are not the bot's to
    # rename).
    updir = ctx.host(UPLOAD_DIR)
    name = UPLOAD_FILE.rsplit("/", 1)[1]
    try:
        dfd = os.open(updir, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_DIRECTORY | os.O_NOFOLLOW)
    except OSError as exc:
        raise Refused(f"{UPLOAD_DIR}: {exc.strerror} — send the archive to the bot again") from None
    try:
        try:
            fd = os.open(name, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_NONBLOCK, dir_fd=dfd)
        except OSError as exc:
            raise Refused(f"{UPLOAD_FILE}: {exc.strerror} — send the archive to the bot again") from None
        with os.fdopen(fd, "rb") as fh:
            st = os.fstat(fh.fileno())
            if not stat.S_ISREG(st.st_mode):
                raise Refused(f"{UPLOAD_FILE} is not a regular file")
            if st.st_size <= 0 or st.st_size > MAX_ARCHIVE_BYTES:
                raise Refused(f"{UPLOAD_FILE}: {st.st_size} bytes (1..{MAX_ARCHIVE_BYTES})")
            data = fh.read(MAX_ARCHIVE_BYTES + 1)
        if len(data) > MAX_ARCHIVE_BYTES:
            raise Refused(f"{UPLOAD_FILE}: more than {MAX_ARCHIVE_BYTES} bytes")
        sha = hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest()
        if not sha.startswith(digest):
            raise Refused("the upload is not the archive this run was started for (its sha256 differs) — send it again")
        archive = work / "archive"
        write_file(ctx, archive, data, 0o600)
        with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
            fence(ctx, updir / name)
            os.unlink(name, dir_fd=dfd)
    finally:
        os.close(dfd)
    return archive, sha


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# State: what is live, what is kept
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
def load_json(path: Path) -> dict[str, Any]:
    try:
        data = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return {}
    return data if isinstance(data, dict) else {}


def load_state(ctx: Ctx) -> dict[str, Any]:
    state = load_json(ctx.host(STATE_FILE))
    releases = [r for r in state.get("releases") or [] if isinstance(r, dict) and re.fullmatch(r"[0-9TZ]+-[0-9a-f]{12}", str(r.get("id") or ""))]
    state["releases"] = [r for r in releases if ctx.host(f"{RELEASES_DIR}/{r['id']}").is_dir()]
    return state


def save_state(ctx: Ctx, state: Mapping[str, Any]) -> None:
    ensure_dir(ctx, ctx.host(STATE_DIR), 0o755)
    write_file(ctx, ctx.host(STATE_FILE), (json.dumps(state, sort_keys=True, indent=1) + "\n").encode(), 0o644)


def load_journal(ctx: Ctx) -> dict[str, Any]:
    return load_json(ctx.host(JOURNAL_FILE))


def save_journal(ctx: Ctx, journal: Mapping[str, Any]) -> None:
    ensure_dir(ctx, ctx.host(STATE_DIR), 0o755)
    write_file(ctx, ctx.host(JOURNAL_FILE), (json.dumps(journal, sort_keys=True, indent=1) + "\n").encode(), 0o600)


def current_record(state: Mapping[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:
    value = state.get("current")
    return dict(value) if isinstance(value, dict) else {}


def revert_target(state: Mapping[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any] | None:
    """The newest kept version that was live before (not one a revert took down)."""
    for rel in reversed(state.get("releases") or []):
        if rel.get("kind") == "previous":
            return dict(rel)
    return None


def work_dir(ctx: Ctx, run_id: int) -> Path:
    return ctx.host(f"{WORK_DIR}/{run_id}")


def stage_paths(site: Site, run_id: int) -> tuple[str, str]:
    parent, name = site.docroot.rsplit("/", 1)
    return f"{parent}/.{name}.vpn-bot-site-{run_id}", f"{parent}/.{name}.vpn-bot-site-{run_id}.old"


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Checks through nginx: TLS (ALPN h2, the domain's certificate) and the pages
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
@dataclass
class Check:
    key: str
    ok: bool
    text: str

    def as_json(self) -> dict[str, Any]:
        return {"key": self.key, "ok": self.ok, "text": self.text}


def check_nginx(ctx: Ctx) -> Check:
    rc, out = run(ctx, ["systemctl", "is-active", NGINX_UNIT])
    active = rc == 0 and out.strip().splitlines()[-1:] == ["active"]
    return Check(f"unit:{NGINX_UNIT}", active, f"{NGINX_UNIT} {'active' if active else 'NOT active'}")


def check_tls(ctx: Ctx, domain: str) -> Check:
    # Not -brief: OpenSSL 3's brief summary leaves the negotiated ALPN out.
    rc, out = run(ctx, ["openssl", "s_client", "-connect", SELFSTEAL_ADDR, "-servername", domain, "-alpn", "h2",
                        "-verify_hostname", domain, "-verify_return_error"], timeout=30, stdin="")
    alpn = bool(re.search(r"^ALPN protocol:\s*h2\b", out, re.MULTILINE))
    verified = rc == 0 and ("Verification: OK" in out or "Verify return code: 0" in out)
    return Check("tls", alpn and verified, f"{SELFSTEAL_ADDR} SNI {domain}: " + ", ".join([
        "the domain's certificate" if verified else "certificate NOT verified for the domain",
        "ALPN h2" if alpn else "no ALPN h2"]))


def check_pages(ctx: Ctx, domain: str, pages: Sequence[str]) -> list[Check]:
    """GET of every page over HTTP/2 with SNI = the domain, through nginx on loopback —
    one curl per batch (one connection), one answer line per URL."""
    checks: list[Check] = []
    for i in range(0, len(pages), CURL_BATCH):
        batch = list(pages[i:i + CURL_BATCH])
        argv = ["curl", "-sS", "--http2", "--max-time", "20", "--resolve", f"{domain}:{SELFSTEAL_PORT}:127.0.0.1",
                "-w", "%{http_code} %{http_version}\\n"]
        for page in batch:
            argv += ["-o", "/dev/null", f"https://{domain}:{SELFSTEAL_PORT}{quote(page, safe='/~._-')}"]
        rc, out = run(ctx, argv, timeout=30 + 5 * len(batch))
        answers = [m.groups() for m in re.finditer(r"^(\d{3}) (\S+)$", out, re.MULTILINE)]
        for n, page in enumerate(batch):
            code, version = answers[n] if n < len(answers) else ("000", "")
            ok = code == "200" and version == "2"
            checks.append(Check(f"page:{page}", ok, f"GET {page} → {code if code != '000' else 'no answer'}"
                                + (f" over HTTP/{version}" if version and version != "0" else "")))
        if rc != 0 and len(answers) < len(batch):
            ctx.log(f"curl exit {rc}: {out.strip()[-300:]}")
    return checks


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# The spiderX pool: the pages of the site (while it is in use)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
def pool_for(pages: Sequence[str]) -> list[str]:
    return [p for p in pages if _POOL_PATH_RE.match(p)][:MAX_POOL]


def spx_keys(ctx: Ctx, pool_after: Sequence[str]) -> tuple[int | None, int | None]:
    """(keys whose stored spx leaves the pool, keys with a stored spx) — read-only (mode=ro:
    the bot owns the database and its WAL; the bot re-lays them, never this helper)."""
    env = read_env(ctx)
    db = ctx.host(env.get("DB_PATH", "").strip() or DEFAULT_DB)
    if not db.is_file():
        return None, None
    try:
        conn = sqlite3.connect(f"file:{quote(str(db))}?mode=ro", uri=True, timeout=5)
        try:
            rows = conn.execute(
                "SELECT spider_x FROM vpn_keys WHERE key_type = 'xray' AND spider_x IS NOT NULL").fetchall()
        finally:
            conn.close()
    except sqlite3.Error as exc:
        ctx.log(f"{ctx.unroot(db)}: {exc}")
        return None, None
    keep = set(pool_after)
    return sum(1 for (value,) in rows if value not in keep), len(rows)


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# PLAN — every change, decided against the host; the sha256 covers the decisions
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
def _diff(old: Tree, new: Tree) -> dict[str, Any]:
    added = sorted(set(new.files) - set(old.files))
    removed = sorted(set(old.files) - set(new.files))
    changed = sorted(r for r in set(new.files) & set(old.files) if new.files[r][0] != old.files[r][0])
    return {"added": added[:50], "removed": removed[:50], "changed": changed[:50],
            "n_added": len(added), "n_removed": len(removed), "n_changed": len(changed),
            "n_same": len(set(new.files) & set(old.files)) - len(changed)}


def _tree_json(tree: Tree) -> dict[str, Any]:
    return {"tree": tree.digest, "files": len(tree.files), "bytes": tree.size, "pages": len(tree.pages()),
            "symlinks": len(tree.symlinks), "complete": tree.complete}


def make_plan(ctx: Ctx, run_id: int, action: str, *, digest: str = "", fresh_upload: bool = False) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """The plan of a run. *fresh_upload*: take the bot's upload into the run's directory
    and unpack it (the plan step); otherwise the run's own unpacked tree is used (apply)."""
    plan: dict[str, Any] = {"version": HELPER_VERSION, "action": action, "run": run_id, "blocking": [], "warnings": [],
                            "checks": [], "nothing_to_do": False}
    site, problems = discover(ctx)
    plan["blocking"] += problems
    if site is None:
        return _seal(plan)
    plan.update(docroot=site.docroot, domain=site.domain, vhost=site.vhost)
    journal = load_journal(ctx)
    if journal.get("state") in ("applying", "applied", "committing"):
        plan["blocking"].append(f"run #{journal.get('run')} left an unfinished change of the site — `vpn-bot-site recover` first")
    state = load_state(ctx)
    current = scan_tree(ctx.host(site.docroot)) if site.exists else Tree()
    if not current.complete:
        plan["blocking"].append(f"{site.docroot}: more than {SCAN_MAX_FILES} files or {SCAN_MAX_BYTES} bytes — not a decoy site this helper replaces")
    cur = current_record(state)
    plan["current"] = {**_tree_json(current), "exists": site.exists, "deployed_at": cur.get("deployed_at"),
                       "known": bool(cur) and cur.get("tree") == current.digest}
    work = work_dir(ctx, run_id)
    new = Tree()
    if action == "deploy":
        if not _DIGEST_RE.match(digest):
            raise Refused("deploy needs --digest: the first 16 hex of the upload's sha256")
        if fresh_upload:
            ensure_dir(ctx, ctx.host(STATE_DIR), 0o755)
            ensure_dir(ctx, ctx.host(WORK_DIR), 0o700)
            ensure_dir(ctx, work, 0o700)
            archive, sha = take_upload(ctx, digest, work)
            unpacked = unpack(ctx, archive, work / "unpacked")
            meta = {"archive": sha, "unwrapped": unpacked.unwrapped, "skipped": unpacked.skipped,
                    "tree_rel": os.path.relpath(unpacked.tree, work)}
            write_file(ctx, work / "upload.json", json.dumps(meta, sort_keys=True).encode(), 0o600)
        meta = load_json(work / "upload.json")
        if not meta.get("tree_rel") or not str(meta.get("archive", "")).startswith(digest):
            raise Refused("this run has no unpacked archive — start it again")
        new_root = work / str(meta["tree_rel"])
        if not os.path.realpath(new_root).startswith(os.path.realpath(work) + "/"):
            raise Refused("the run's unpacked tree is outside its directory")
        new = scan_tree(new_root)
        plan["new"] = {**_tree_json(new), "archive": meta["archive"], "unwrapped": meta.get("unwrapped") or "",
                       "skipped": meta.get("skipped") or 0, "source": "upload"}
        plan["source_dir"] = ctx.unroot(new_root)
    elif action == "revert":
        target = revert_target(state)
        if target is None:
            plan["blocking"].append("no kept version to go back to (the first deploy keeps the one it replaces)")
            return _seal(plan)
        rel_dir = ctx.host(f"{RELEASES_DIR}/{target['id']}")
        new = scan_tree(rel_dir)
        plan["new"] = {**_tree_json(new), "release": target["id"], "deployed_at": target.get("deployed_at"),
                       "archive": target.get("archive"), "source": "revert"}
        plan["source_dir"] = ctx.unroot(rel_dir)
        if new.digest != target.get("tree"):
            plan["warnings"].append(f"the kept version {target['id']} differs from what was recorded when it was kept")
        if not (rel_dir / "index.html").is_file():
            plan["blocking"].append(f"the kept version {target['id']} has no index.html")
    else:
        raise Refused(f"unknown action {action!r}")
    plan["diff"] = _diff(current, new)
    old_pages, new_pages = current.pages(), new.pages()
    plan["pages"] = {"before": len(old_pages), "after": len(new_pages),
                     "added": [p for p in new_pages if p not in set(old_pages)][:50],
                     "removed": [p for p in old_pages if p not in set(new_pages)][:50],
                     "list": new_pages[:MAX_LISTED]}
    pool_before = parse_pool(read_env(ctx).get(POOL_KEY))
    enabled = bool(pool_before)
    pool_after = pool_for(new_pages) if enabled else []
    changed = enabled and set(pool_after) != set(pool_before)
    moved, with_spx = spx_keys(ctx, pool_after) if changed else (0, None)
    plan["spx"] = {"enabled": enabled, "before": pool_before, "after": pool_after if changed else pool_before,
                   "changed": changed, "added": [p for p in pool_after if p not in set(pool_before)] if changed else [],
                   "removed": [p for p in pool_before if p not in set(pool_after)] if changed else [],
                   "keys_moved": moved, "keys_with_spx": with_spx}
    if enabled and not pool_after:
        plan["blocking"].append("the new site has no page a spiderX path can name, and XRAY_SPIDER_X_POOL is in use")
    # The store after commit: the replaced tree is added (when there was one), the version
    # a revert takes is removed from it, the oldest go past KEEP_RELEASES (commit's prune).
    taken = plan["new"].get("release")
    after = [r for r in state.get("releases") or [] if r.get("id") != taken]
    n_after = len(after) + (1 if site.exists else 0)
    plan["store"] = {"keep": KEEP_RELEASES, "kept": len(state.get("releases") or []),
                     "save_as": ("previous" if action == "deploy" else "rolled_back") if site.exists else None,
                     "drop": [str(r["id"]) for r in after[: max(0, n_after - KEEP_RELEASES)]]}
    plan["hy2"] = hy2_layout(ctx)
    if plan["hy2"]["layout"] == "file":
        plan["warnings"].append(f"Hysteria2's masquerade reads its own copy ({plan['hy2']['detail'] or '?'}, type: file): "
                                "it shows the new site only once deploy/vpn-bot-decoy-freshen.sh mirrored it")
    elif plan["hy2"]["layout"] == "other":
        plan["warnings"].append(f"Hysteria2's masquerade proxies to {plan['hy2']['detail']}, not to {SELFSTEAL_ADDR}")
    if current.symlinks:
        plan["warnings"].append(f"the live site has {len(current.symlinks)} symlink(s): they are kept with the old version, the new one has none")
    if new.files and new.digest == current.digest:
        plan["nothing_to_do"] = True
    if not plan["blocking"] and not plan["nothing_to_do"]:
        # The self-steal must answer right BEFORE the change, or a failed verify would
        # roll back a site that was not the problem.
        nginx = check_nginx(ctx)
        tls = check_tls(ctx, site.domain)
        plan["checks"] = [nginx.as_json(), tls.as_json()]
        if not nginx.ok:
            plan["blocking"].append(f"{NGINX_UNIT} is not active — the site has nobody serving it")
        elif not tls.ok:
            plan["blocking"].append(f"the self-steal does not answer as it must before the change ({tls.text}) — "
                                    "fix the certificate first («🔐 Сертификат и DNS»)")
        elif site.exists:
            (root_page,) = check_pages(ctx, site.domain, ["/"])
            plan["checks"].append(root_page.as_json())
            if not root_page.ok:
                plan["warnings"].append(f"the live site answers {root_page.text}")
    plan["release_id"] = f"{time.strftime('%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ', time.gmtime())}-{(current.digest or '0' * 12)[:12]}"
    return _seal(plan)


def _seal(plan: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:
    decisions = {k: plan.get(k) for k in ("action", "docroot", "domain", "blocking", "nothing_to_do")}
    decisions["current"] = (plan.get("current") or {}).get("tree")
    decisions["new"] = (plan.get("new") or {}).get("tree")
    decisions["release"] = (plan.get("new") or {}).get("release")
    decisions["pool"] = (plan.get("spx") or {}).get("after")
    decisions["drop"] = (plan.get("store") or {}).get("drop")
    plan["sha256"] = hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(decisions, sort_keys=True).encode()).hexdigest()
    return plan


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# APPLY: stage → swap → .env, journaled; ROLLBACK backwards
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
def fault(ctx: Ctx, step: str) -> None:
    if SELFTEST and ctx.fail_at == step:
        raise StepFailed(step, f"selftest: failing after {step}")


def step_stage(ctx: Ctx, plan: Mapping[str, Any], journal: dict[str, Any]) -> None:
    stage = ctx.host(journal["stage"])
    if stage.exists() or stage.is_symlink():
        remove_tree(ctx, stage)
    journal["staged"] = True
    save_journal(ctx, journal)
    src = ctx.host(str(plan["source_dir"]))
    if plan["action"] == "deploy":
        # 0644 / 0755, root:root (the helper's own files): nothing of the archive's modes.
        fence(ctx, stage)
        os.mkdir(stage, 0o700)
        for cur, dirs, files in os.walk(src, followlinks=False):
            rel = os.path.relpath(cur, src)
            target_dir = stage if rel == "." else stage / rel
            for d in sorted(dirs):
                if os.path.islink(os.path.join(cur, d)):
                    raise StepFailed("site_stage", f"{rel}/{d}: a symlink in the unpacked tree")
                os.mkdir(target_dir / d, 0o755)
                os.chmod(target_dir / d, 0o755)  # noqa: S103 — a directory of the site: nginx reads it
            for f in sorted(files):
                s = Path(cur) / f
                if not stat.S_ISREG(os.lstat(s).st_mode):
                    raise StepFailed("site_stage", f"{rel}/{f}: not a regular file in the unpacked tree")
                shutil.copyfile(s, target_dir / f, follow_symlinks=False)
                os.chmod(target_dir / f, 0o644)
        os.chmod(stage, 0o755)  # noqa: S103 — a directory of the site: nginx reads it
    else:
        copy_tree(ctx, src, stage)
    tree = scan_tree(stage)
    if tree.digest != plan["new"]["tree"]:
        raise StepFailed("site_stage", "the staged tree is not the planned one")
    fault(ctx, "site_stage")


def step_swap(ctx: Ctx, plan: Mapping[str, Any], journal: dict[str, Any]) -> None:
    docroot = ctx.host(str(plan["docroot"]))
    stage = ctx.host(journal["stage"])
    if not (docroot.exists() or docroot.is_symlink()):
        journal["swap"] = "created"
        save_journal(ctx, journal)
        os.rename(stage, docroot)
    else:
        journal["swap"] = "exchanging"
        save_journal(ctx, journal)
        if exchange(ctx, stage, docroot):
            journal["swap"] = "exchanged"
            journal["old"] = journal["stage"]
            journal["atomic"] = True
        else:
            journal["swap"] = "moving"
            journal["old"] = journal["old_path"]
            journal["atomic"] = False
            save_journal(ctx, journal)
            os.rename(docroot, ctx.host(journal["old_path"]))
            journal["swap"] = "moved"
            save_journal(ctx, journal)
            os.rename(stage, docroot)
            journal["swap"] = "renamed"
    save_journal(ctx, journal)
    fault(ctx, "site_swap")


def step_env(ctx: Ctx, plan: Mapping[str, Any], journal: dict[str, Any]) -> bool:
    spx = plan.get("spx") or {}
    if not spx.get("changed"):
        return False
    path = ctx.host(ENV_FILE)
    try:
        st = os.stat(path)
        before = path.read_bytes()
    except OSError as exc:
        raise StepFailed("site_env", f"{ENV_FILE}: {exc.strerror}") from None
    backup = work_dir(ctx, int(plan["run"])) / "env.before"
    write_file(ctx, backup, before, 0o600)
    journal["env"] = {"backup": ctx.unroot(backup), "mode": stat.S_IMODE(st.st_mode), "uid": st.st_uid, "gid": st.st_gid}
    save_journal(ctx, journal)
    text = edit_env_text(before.decode("utf-8", errors="surrogateescape"), {POOL_KEY: ",".join(spx["after"])})
    write_file(ctx, path, text.encode("utf-8", errors="surrogateescape"), stat.S_IMODE(st.st_mode), uid=st.st_uid, gid=st.st_gid)
    fault(ctx, "site_env")
    return True


def rollback_journal(ctx: Ctx, journal: dict[str, Any]) -> list[str]:
    """Undo whatever the journal says was done, newest first. Returns the errors."""
    errors: list[str] = []
    env = journal.get("env")
    if isinstance(env, dict) and env.get("backup"):
        try:
            data = ctx.host(str(env["backup"])).read_bytes()
            write_file(ctx, ctx.host(ENV_FILE), data, int(env.get("mode", 0o600)), uid=env.get("uid"), gid=env.get("gid"))
            journal["env"] = None
            save_journal(ctx, journal)
        except OSError as exc:
            errors.append(f".env not restored: {exc}")
    if "state_before" in journal:
        # commit had begun: state.json back as it was (no file: none again).
        try:
            before = journal["state_before"]
            if before:
                save_state(ctx, before)
            else:
                with contextlib.suppress(FileNotFoundError):
                    fence(ctx, ctx.host(STATE_FILE))
                    ctx.host(STATE_FILE).unlink()
            del journal["state_before"]
            save_journal(ctx, journal)
        except OSError as exc:
            errors.append(f"state.json not restored: {exc}")
    docroot = ctx.host(str(journal["docroot"]))
    stage = ctx.host(str(journal["stage"]))
    old_at = journal.get("old_at")
    try:
        if old_at and journal.get("old") and old_at != journal["old"]:
            # commit had kept the old tree already: bring it back next to the docroot first.
            move_tree(ctx, ctx.host(old_at), ctx.host(journal["old"]))
            journal["old_at"] = None
            save_journal(ctx, journal)
        swap = journal.get("swap")
        if swap == "exchanged":
            if not exchange(ctx, stage, docroot):
                tmp = ctx.host(str(journal["old_path"]) + ".new")
                os.rename(docroot, tmp)
                os.rename(stage, docroot)
                remove_tree(ctx, tmp)
            else:
                remove_tree(ctx, stage)
        elif swap in ("renamed", "moved", "moving"):
            old = ctx.host(str(journal["old_path"]))
            if swap == "renamed":
                os.rename(docroot, stage)
            if old.exists():
                os.rename(old, docroot)
        elif swap == "created":
            if docroot.exists():
                os.rename(docroot, stage)
        elif swap == "exchanging" and stage.exists():
            # Killed in the very step: the exchange happened when the stage holds the OLD tree.
            planned_new = journal.get("new_tree")
            if planned_new and scan_tree(docroot).digest == planned_new:
                if not exchange(ctx, stage, docroot):
                    errors.append("cannot exchange back: no RENAME_EXCHANGE")
        journal["swap"] = None
        save_journal(ctx, journal)
        if stage.exists() or stage.is_symlink():
            remove_tree(ctx, stage)
    except OSError as exc:
        errors.append(f"the site not swapped back: {exc}")
    return errors


def cleanup_work(ctx: Ctx, run_id: int) -> None:
    with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
        remove_tree(ctx, work_dir(ctx, run_id))


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Verbs
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
def out(ctx: Ctx, result: Mapping[str, Any], text: str) -> None:
    if ctx.json_out:
        print(json.dumps(result, sort_keys=True), flush=True)
    else:
        print(text)


def cmd_status(ctx: Ctx) -> int:
    site, problems = discover(ctx)
    state = load_state(ctx)
    journal = load_journal(ctx)
    result: dict[str, Any] = {"version": HELPER_VERSION, "problems": problems, "hy2": hy2_layout(ctx),
                              "limits": {"archive": MAX_ARCHIVE_BYTES, "files": MAX_FILES, "bytes": MAX_TOTAL_BYTES,
                                         "file": MAX_FILE_BYTES, "depth": MAX_DEPTH, "ext": sorted(STATIC_EXT),
                                         "keep": KEEP_RELEASES},
                              "journal": {"run": journal.get("run"), "state": journal.get("state")} if journal else None}
    pool = parse_pool(read_env(ctx).get(POOL_KEY))
    if site is not None:
        tree = scan_tree(ctx.host(site.docroot)) if site.exists else Tree()
        pages = tree.pages()
        cur = current_record(state)
        known = bool(cur) and bool(cur.get("tree"))
        result.update(docroot=site.docroot, domain=site.domain, vhost=site.vhost, exists=site.exists)
        result["current"] = {
            **_tree_json(tree),
            "deployed_at": cur.get("deployed_at") if known else None,
            "run": cur.get("run") if known else None,
            "source": cur.get("source") if known else "host",
            "archive": cur.get("archive") if known else None,
            "modified": known and cur.get("tree") != tree.digest,
            "newest_mtime": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime(tree.newest)) if tree.newest else None,
        }
        result["pages"] = pages[:MAX_LISTED]
        result["pages_total"] = len(pages)
        missing = [p for p in pool if p not in set(pages)]
        result["spx"] = {"enabled": bool(pool), "pool": pool, "missing": missing,
                         "in_sync": bool(pool) and not missing and set(pool) == set(pool_for(pages))}
    else:
        result["spx"] = {"enabled": bool(pool), "pool": pool, "missing": [], "in_sync": False}
    result["releases"] = [{k: r.get(k) for k in ("id", "tree", "pages", "files", "bytes", "kind", "stored_at",
                                                    "deployed_at", "source")} for r in state.get("releases") or []]
    target = revert_target(state)
    result["revert_to"] = target["id"] if target else None
    result["ok"] = site is not None and not problems
    text = [f"site: {result.get('docroot', '?')} ({result.get('domain', '?')})"]
    if "current" in result:
        c = result["current"]
        text.append(f"version: {str(c['tree'])[:12] or '?'} · {c['pages']} page(s), {c['files']} file(s) · "
                    f"deployed {c['deployed_at'] or 'by hand'}")
    text += [f"problem: {p}" for p in problems]
    text.append(f"kept: {', '.join(r['id'] for r in result['releases']) or 'none'}")
    out(ctx, result, "\n".join(text))
    return EXIT_OK if result["ok"] else EXIT_REFUSED


def plan_text(plan: Mapping[str, Any]) -> str:
    lines = [f"{plan.get('action')} {plan.get('docroot', '?')} ({plan.get('domain', '?')}) · plan {str(plan.get('sha256'))[:12]}"]
    for b in plan.get("blocking") or []:
        lines.append(f"⛔ {b}")
    return "\n".join(lines)


def prune_work(ctx: Ctx, keep_run: int) -> None:
    """The directories of earlier runs: one run at a time holds the wizard's lock, so a
    plan that was cancelled or expired left its unpacked archive behind — never the one of
    an unfinished journal (recover takes it)."""
    base = ctx.host(WORK_DIR)
    if not base.is_dir() or base.is_symlink():
        return
    journal = load_journal(ctx)
    open_run = journal.get("run") if journal.get("state") not in ("committed", "rolled_back", "recovered") else None
    for entry in base.iterdir():
        if entry.name.isdigit() and int(entry.name) not in (keep_run, open_run):
            with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
                remove_tree(ctx, entry)


def cmd_plan(ctx: Ctx, run_id: int, action: str, digest: str) -> int:
    with helper_lock(ctx):
        prune_work(ctx, run_id)
        cleanup_work(ctx, run_id)
        try:
            plan = make_plan(ctx, run_id, action, digest=digest, fresh_upload=action == "deploy")
        except Refused:
            cleanup_work(ctx, run_id)
            raise
        if plan["blocking"] or plan["nothing_to_do"]:
            # Nothing will be applied: the unpacked archive goes now.
            cleanup_work(ctx, run_id)
        else:
            work = work_dir(ctx, run_id)
            ensure_dir(ctx, ctx.host(STATE_DIR), 0o755)
            ensure_dir(ctx, ctx.host(WORK_DIR), 0o700)
            ensure_dir(ctx, work, 0o700)
            write_file(ctx, work / "plan.json", json.dumps(plan, sort_keys=True).encode(), 0o600)
    out(ctx, plan, plan_text(plan))
    return EXIT_REFUSED if plan["blocking"] else EXIT_OK


def cmd_apply(ctx: Ctx, run_id: int, expect: str) -> int:
    if not _SHA_RE.match(expect):
        raise Refused("--expect-plan must be the plan's sha256")
    with helper_lock(ctx):
        saved = load_json(work_dir(ctx, run_id) / "plan.json")
        if not saved:
            raise Refused("no plan of this run — plan it first")
        new = saved.get("new") or {}
        digest = str(new.get("archive") or "")[:16] if saved.get("action") == "deploy" else ""
        plan = make_plan(ctx, run_id, str(saved.get("action")), digest=digest)
        if plan["blocking"]:
            out(ctx, {"ok": False, "error": "blocked", "blocking": plan["blocking"]}, "\n".join(plan["blocking"]))
            return EXIT_REFUSED
        if plan["sha256"] != expect:
            out(ctx, {"ok": False, "error": "plan_changed", "detail": "the site, the archive or the pool changed since the plan"},
                "the plan changed: nothing was done — plan it again")
            return EXIT_REFUSED
        if plan["nothing_to_do"]:
            out(ctx, {"ok": True, "nothing_to_do": True}, "nothing to do: the site already is this version")
            return EXIT_OK
        site = Site(docroot=plan["docroot"], domain=plan["domain"], vhost=plan["vhost"], exists=plan["current"]["exists"])
        stage, old_path = stage_paths(site, run_id)
        journal: dict[str, Any] = {"run": run_id, "action": plan["action"], "state": "applying", "docroot": plan["docroot"],
                                   "stage": stage, "old_path": old_path, "old": None, "old_at": None, "swap": None,
                                   "env": None, "new_tree": plan["new"]["tree"], "started": iso_now()}
        save_journal(ctx, journal)
        current_step = ""
        env_changed = False
        try:
            for name in APPLY_STEPS:
                current_step = name
                ctx.event(event="step", step=name, state="run")
                if name == "site_stage":
                    step_stage(ctx, plan, journal)
                elif name == "site_swap":
                    step_swap(ctx, plan, journal)
                else:
                    env_changed = step_env(ctx, plan, journal)
                ctx.event(event="step", step=name, state="ok" if name != "site_env" or env_changed else "skip")
        except (StepFailed, OSError, Refused, Cannot) as exc:
            ctx.event(event="step", step=current_step, state="fail")
            detail = str(exc)
            ctx.log(f"apply: {current_step} failed: {detail}")
            errors = rollback_journal(ctx, journal)
            journal["state"] = "rolled_back" if not errors else "rollback_failed"
            journal["errors"] = errors
            save_journal(ctx, journal)
            if not errors:
                cleanup_work(ctx, run_id)
            out(ctx, {"ok": False, "error": "step_failed", "failed_step": current_step, "detail": detail,
                      "rollback_errors": errors}, f"{current_step} failed: {detail}; rolled back"
                + (f" INCOMPLETELY: {'; '.join(errors)}" if errors else ""))
            return EXIT_ROLLED_BACK if not errors else EXIT_ROLLBACK_FAILED
        journal["state"] = "applied"
        save_journal(ctx, journal)
    out(ctx, {"ok": True, "atomic": journal.get("atomic", True), "env_changed": env_changed, "docroot": plan["docroot"],
              "tree": plan["new"]["tree"], "pool": plan["spx"]["after"] if env_changed else None},
        f"the site is {plan['new']['tree'][:12]} ({'one atomic exchange' if journal.get('atomic', True) else 'two renames'})")
    return EXIT_OK


def cmd_verify(ctx: Ctx, run_id: int) -> int:
    plan = load_json(work_dir(ctx, run_id) / "plan.json")
    if not plan:
        raise Refused("no plan of this run")
    journal = load_journal(ctx)
    checks: list[Check] = []
    docroot = ctx.host(str(plan["docroot"]))
    tree = scan_tree(docroot)
    checks.append(Check("tree", tree.digest == plan["new"]["tree"],
                        f"{plan['docroot']} is {tree.digest[:12] or '?'}" + ("" if tree.digest == plan["new"]["tree"]
                                                                            else f", the plan's is {plan['new']['tree'][:12]}")))
    checks.append(check_nginx(ctx))
    checks.append(check_tls(ctx, str(plan["domain"])))
    pages = tree.pages()
    if "/" not in pages:
        checks.append(Check("page:/", False, "the site has no index.html"))
    checks += check_pages(ctx, str(plan["domain"]), pages)
    spx = plan.get("spx") or {}
    if spx.get("changed"):
        now = parse_pool(read_env(ctx).get(POOL_KEY))
        checks.append(Check("spx_pool", now == list(spx["after"]),
                            f"{POOL_KEY}: {len(now)} path(s) of the new site" if now == list(spx["after"])
                            else f"{POOL_KEY} is not the planned pool"))
    ok = all(c.ok for c in checks)
    out(ctx, {"ok": ok, "checks": [c.as_json() for c in checks], "journal": journal.get("state")},
        "\n".join(f"{'ok ' if c.ok else 'FAIL'} {c.key}: {c.text}" for c in checks))
    return EXIT_OK if ok else EXIT_VERIFY


def prune(ctx: Ctx, state: dict[str, Any]) -> list[str]:
    releases = list(state.get("releases") or [])
    dropped = []
    while len(releases) > KEEP_RELEASES:
        rel = releases.pop(0)
        with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
            remove_tree(ctx, ctx.host(f"{RELEASES_DIR}/{rel['id']}"))
        dropped.append(str(rel["id"]))
    state["releases"] = releases
    return dropped


def cmd_commit(ctx: Ctx, run_id: int) -> int:
    with helper_lock(ctx):
        journal = load_journal(ctx)
        if journal.get("run") != run_id or journal.get("state") not in ("applied", "committing"):
            raise Refused(f"no applied change of run #{run_id} to commit (journal: {journal.get('state') or 'none'})")
        plan = load_json(work_dir(ctx, run_id) / "plan.json")
        if not plan:
            raise Refused("no plan of this run")
        state = load_state(ctx)
        journal["state"] = "committing"
        journal["state_before"] = load_json(ctx.host(STATE_FILE))
        save_journal(ctx, journal)
        warnings: list[str] = []
        now = iso_now()
        old = journal.get("old")
        cur = plan["current"]
        prior = current_record(state)
        if old and ctx.host(old).is_dir():
            ensure_dir(ctx, ctx.host(RELEASES_DIR), 0o700)
            rid = str(plan.get("release_id") or f"{time.strftime('%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ', time.gmtime())}-{'0' * 12}")
            target = ctx.host(f"{RELEASES_DIR}/{rid}")
            if target.exists():
                rid = f"{rid[:-12]}{hashlib.sha256((rid + now).encode()).hexdigest()[:12]}"
                target = ctx.host(f"{RELEASES_DIR}/{rid}")
            move_tree(ctx, ctx.host(old), target)
            journal["old_at"] = ctx.unroot(target)
            save_journal(ctx, journal)
            entry = {"id": rid, "tree": cur["tree"], "pages": cur["pages"], "files": cur["files"], "bytes": cur["bytes"],
                     "kind": "previous" if plan["action"] == "deploy" else "rolled_back", "stored_at": now,
                     "deployed_at": prior.get("deployed_at") if cur.get("known") else None,
                     "archive": prior.get("archive") if cur.get("known") else None,
                     "source": (prior.get("source") or "bot") if cur.get("known") else "host"}
            state["releases"] = [*state.get("releases", []), entry]
        taken = (plan.get("new") or {}).get("release")
        if taken:
            state["releases"] = [r for r in state.get("releases", []) if r.get("id") != taken]
        new = plan["new"]
        state["current"] = {"tree": new["tree"], "pages": new["pages"], "files": new["files"], "bytes": new["bytes"],
                            "deployed_at": now, "run": run_id, "source": new.get("source"),
                            "archive": new.get("archive"), "release": taken}
        state["docroot"] = plan["docroot"]
        state["version"] = HELPER_VERSION
        fault(ctx, "commit")
        save_state(ctx, state)
        journal["state"] = "committed"
        journal["committed"] = now
        journal.pop("state_before", None)
        save_journal(ctx, journal)
        # Past the point of no return: only tidying (a failure is a warning, the site stands).
        if taken:
            try:
                remove_tree(ctx, ctx.host(f"{RELEASES_DIR}/{taken}"))
            except OSError as exc:
                warnings.append(f"the kept copy {taken} could not be removed: {exc}")
        dropped = prune(ctx, state)
        if dropped:
            try:
                save_state(ctx, state)
            except OSError as exc:
                warnings.append(f"state.json after the prune: {exc}")
        cleanup_work(ctx, run_id)
    spx = plan.get("spx") or {}
    out(ctx, {"ok": True, "kept": journal.get("old_at"), "dropped": dropped, "warnings": warnings,
              "pool_changed": bool(spx.get("changed")), "pool": spx.get("after") if spx.get("changed") else None},
        f"committed; kept {journal.get('old_at') or 'nothing'}; dropped {', '.join(dropped) or 'nothing'}")
    return EXIT_OK


def cmd_rollback(ctx: Ctx, run_id: int | None) -> int:
    with helper_lock(ctx):
        journal = load_journal(ctx)
        if not journal or (run_id is not None and journal.get("run") != run_id) or \
                journal.get("state") in ("committed", "rolled_back", "recovered"):
            if run_id is not None:
                cleanup_work(ctx, run_id)
            out(ctx, {"ok": True, "nothing_to_do": True, "journal": journal.get("state")}, "nothing to roll back")
            return EXIT_OK
        errors = rollback_journal(ctx, journal)
        journal["state"] = ("rolled_back" if run_id is not None else "recovered") if not errors else "rollback_failed"
        journal["errors"] = errors
        save_journal(ctx, journal)
        if not errors:
            cleanup_work(ctx, int(journal.get("run") or 0))
    out(ctx, {"ok": not errors, "rollback_errors": errors, "run": journal.get("run")},
        "rolled back" if not errors else "rollback incomplete: " + "; ".join(errors))
    return EXIT_OK if not errors else EXIT_ROLLBACK_FAILED


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# CLI
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
def parse_args(argv: Sequence[str]) -> argparse.Namespace:
    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="vpn-bot-site", add_help=True)
    sub = p.add_subparsers(dest="verb", required=True)

    def run_arg(sp: argparse.ArgumentParser, required: bool = True) -> None:
        sp.add_argument("--run", type=int, required=required)

    s = sub.add_parser("status")
    s.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    s = sub.add_parser("plan")
    s.add_argument("action", choices=("deploy", "revert"))
    run_arg(s)
    s.add_argument("--digest", default="")
    s.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    s = sub.add_parser("apply")
    run_arg(s)
    s.add_argument("--expect-plan", required=True)
    s.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    for verb in ("verify", "commit", "rollback"):
        s = sub.add_parser(verb)
        run_arg(s)
        s.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    s = sub.add_parser("recover")
    s.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    ns = p.parse_args(list(argv))
    run_id = getattr(ns, "run", None)
    if run_id is not None and not 0 < run_id < 10**9:
        p.error("--run must be a positive integer")
    return ns


def main(argv: Sequence[str]) -> int:
    try:
        ns = parse_args(argv)
    except SystemExit as exc:
        return EXIT_USAGE if exc.code else EXIT_OK
    ctx: Ctx | None = None
    try:
        if os.geteuid() != 0 and not SELFTEST:
            raise Refused("run as root")
        c = ctx = make_ctx(bool(getattr(ns, "json", False)))
        handlers: dict[str, Callable[[], int]] = {
            "status": lambda: cmd_status(c),
            "plan": lambda: cmd_plan(c, ns.run, ns.action, ns.digest),
            "apply": lambda: cmd_apply(c, ns.run, ns.expect_plan),
            "verify": lambda: cmd_verify(c, ns.run),
            "commit": lambda: cmd_commit(c, ns.run),
            "rollback": lambda: cmd_rollback(c, ns.run),
            "recover": lambda: cmd_rollback(c, None),
        }
        c.log(f"--- vpn-bot-site {' '.join(argv)}")
        return handlers[ns.verb]()
    except Refused as exc:
        return _fail(ctx, EXIT_REFUSED, "refused", str(exc))
    except Cannot as exc:
        return _fail(ctx, EXIT_CANNOT, "cannot", str(exc))
    except OSError as exc:
        return _fail(ctx, EXIT_CANNOT, "cannot", f"{exc.strerror or exc}: {exc.filename or ''}".rstrip(": "))


def _fail(ctx: Ctx | None, code: int, kind: str, detail: str) -> int:
    if ctx is not None:
        ctx.log(f"{kind}: {detail}")
        if ctx.json_out:
            print(json.dumps({"ok": False, "error": kind, "detail": redact(detail), "blocking": [redact(detail)]}), flush=True)
            return code
    print(f"vpn-bot-site: {kind}: {redact(detail)}", file=sys.stderr)
    return code


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
